   610	// P1T-FIX3, round-3 review finding V3-02: the pending-list byte total is SATURATING. note_push / note_pop run inside the
   611	// noexcept RetainUntilComplete destructor and the drain loops, so they may neither throw nor drain; an unchecked
   612	// signed addition here was undefined behaviour for near-limit totals (review probe pending_bytes queue: 4 +
   613	// 9223372036854775804), and a wrapped negative total could have suppressed the bound drain.
   614	//  * Push: checked addition; on overflow the total is pinned at INT64_MAX and marked saturated (counted). Every entry's
   615	//    own bytes is a checked int64 sum >= 0 (aggregate_operand_bytes, before the launch), so only the queue total can
   616	//    overflow.
   617	//  * Pop: exact subtraction while not saturated (the total is then the exact sum of the queued entries, so it never
   618	//    goes below 0); while saturated the total stays pinned at INT64_MAX until the list is empty, where the true total is
   619	//    0 again. A pinned total over-reports, never under-reports, so the bound comparison (pending_over_bound) is exact
   620	//    below INT64_MAX and conservative above it: a push that would overflow always drains, as the exact arithmetic would
   621	//    have (any total above INT64_MAX is far above kPendingMaxBytes).
   622	// Chosen over drain-before-add because these functions are pure accounting: draining runs producer deleters (Python,
   623	// possibly re-entering tc_signal) and cannot run in the middle of a push; and a drain cannot guarantee headroom anyway
   624	// (entries pushed by a re-entrant call during the drain stay queued), so a non-throwing, non-overflowing rule is needed
   625	// in any case. Saturation is that rule; the drain itself is left to the bound comparison right after the push.
   626	// Prior art: saturating arithmetic (DSP/SIMD saturated add, e.g. Intel MMX/SSE PADDS, 1997-; ARM QADD) and the checked
   627	// builtins it is built from (GCC 5 __builtin_add_overflow, 2015; C23 ckd_add); SEI CERT INT32-C. Taken: checked
   628	// add with a saturated result. Ours: the sticky saturated state that is cleared only when the list empties, so pops
   629	// never make a saturated total under-report. Unverified here (lead to check): "PADDSW saturating add MMX 1997".
   630	void note_push(PendingState& st, const PendingEntry& e) noexcept {
   631	  int64_t sum = 0;
   632	  if (!st.bytes_saturated && __builtin_add_overflow(st.bytes, e.bytes, &sum)) {
   633	    st.bytes_saturated = true;
   634	    ++st.bytes_saturations;
   635	  }
   636	  st.bytes = st.bytes_saturated ? std::numeric_limits<int64_t>::max() : sum;
   637	  st.managers += static_cast<long long>(e.owners.size());
   638	  ++st.retained_entries;
   639	  st.high_water_entries = std::max<long long>(st.high_water_entries, static_cast<long long>(st.q.size()));
   640	  st.high_water_managers = std::max(st.high_water_managers, st.managers);
   641	  st.high_water_bytes = std::max(st.high_water_bytes, st.bytes);
   642	}
