docs/P1T_REV3_REPORT.md:48:### V3-01 — MAJOR: shutdown timeout resumes finalization with admitted releases still using Python
docs/P1T_REV3_REPORT.md:62:This is a finite callback, not an assertion about a producer that never returns. FIX2's bounded regression proves timing/reporting before immediate process exit; it bypasses normal finalization. The FIX2 report acknowledges a timeout residual, but that residual keeps F04/N5 open under this review's merge standard. The full real-Storage probe is `probes/core_exit_overrun.py`, pending for the lead; the CPU slice already settles the review finding.
docs/P1T_REV3_REPORT.md:66:Origin: incomplete FIX2 N5 closure, not an independently proved ordinary-operation regression. Prior art: CPython 3.12 GIL/finalization semantics and the standard admission-counter and quiescence rule; C++17 cleanup boundaries. Taken: those lifecycle constraints. This review contributes the finite-overrun normal-exit scenario. [CPython 3.12 lifecycle docs](https://docs.python.org/3.12/c-api/init.html), [pinned3.12.3 GIL source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/v3.12.3/Python/ceval_gil.c).
docs/P1T_REV3_REPORT.md:68:### V3-02 — MINOR: aggregate retained-byte accounting is unchecked
docs/P1T_REV3_REPORT.md:79:Receipt: `pending_bytes_results.json`, `probes/pending_bytes.cpp`. This establishes host arithmetic UB for the accepted metadata, not the existence of exabyte GPU arrays or a full kernel-launch reproduction. MINOR reflects that practical hardware reachability limit. Under wrapping execution, a negative accounting value can suppress the256 MiB bound check; ordinary representable aggregates work.
docs/P1T_REV3_REPORT.md:83:## R1–R6 reasoning
docs/P1T_REV3_REPORT.md:85:R1 RISK: ordinary core allocation/free branches and existing kernel bodies are preserved; external fields default null, and existing revision/offset behavior is unchanged. FIX2 numel/stride helpers agree with baseline on representable supported shapes and replace overflowing products with exceptions. Nevertheless the new imported-Storage lifecycle has V3-01 and the native Storage ABI requires coordinated rebuilds. No claim of a newly failing baseline suite case.
docs/P1T_REV3_REPORT.md:87:R2 UNSOUND: manager ownership, used_* names, RAII export context, byte_offset, contiguous/singleton checks, dtype/flags, event fence and device-correct external teardown are structurally sound in their reviewed ordinary paths. Bare capsules carry the caller's stream-ordering obligation. Admission closes the ordinary shutdown race, but V3-01 prevents lifecycle soundness. GPU fence/offset/multi-device behavior is not executed here.
docs/P1T_REV3_REPORT.md:89:R3 UNSOUND at the required near-limit robustness boundary: consumed managers survive success and partial launches via events, fallback sync proves completion before release, and failed completion deliberately leaks. Entries are removed before reentrant deleters, with no queue reference carried across callbacks. Allocation failure is caught on queue push, recycle capacity is preallocated, and state is initialized at import. CUDA failures returned by query/sync are surfaced, and ordinary throwing deleters are contained per manager. V3-02 leaves aggregate arithmetic outside the checked contract. No ordinary-sized premature-release defect found; GPU OOM/pending/multi-device/last-error-slot cases remain probes, not guessed passes.
docs/P1T_REV3_REPORT.md:91:R4 DEFECTS for V3-02 aggregate arithmetic. All plan functions and kernel equations were read. Positive validated fp32 byte bounds also bound kernel pointer/index intermediates; convolution and LSTM cuBLAS casts are checked. Conv grouped SGEMM dimensions/layout, ConvTranspose gather tap condition, LSTM ONNX i/o/f/c gates/bias halves/reverse indexing, norm affine indices/centered variance/reduction barriers, exact integer nearest/reflect maps and rintf rounding match their contracts by source reasoning. Zero dimensions are intentionally refused by add-on; scalar rint is accepted. Extreme fp32 norm-statistic overflow is not broader finite-data certification. No new core __global__ kernel or modification to core round was introduced. Numerical/determinism probes remain finite GPU gates.
docs/P1T_REV3_REPORT.md:95:R6 REJECT: V3-01 is an open MAJOR. Passing finite fixtures, historical regression IDs, or the source closure of other items cannot turn the unexercised timeout finalization into an approval. Correct it, verify normal full-path exit, rerun the unchanged relevant gates against rebuilt binaries, and review again.
