docs/P1T_FIX2_REPORT.md:36:| **N3** `bad_alloc` in the release path called std::terminate | `dlpack_operand.cpp`:<br>• `:644` the in-place two-phase sync makes no allocation (no take-all deque, no std::set or std::vector; fixed-capacity `DeviceSyncSet` `:520` / `SyncReport`)<br>• `:686` `acquire_event` reserves the event's pool slot when the event is created (constructor path)<br>• `:584` `recycle_event` never allocates and is caught<br>• `:747` the pending push is caught and falls back to a synchronous release (counted)<br>• `:720` owner vector reserved in the constructor<br>• `:714` `init_pending_state()` at import (`bindings.cpp:410`)<br>• `:831` message building -> MemoryError | `test_fix2_findings.py`:<br>• `:386` named sites, each in its own process: owner_reserve, event_pool_reserve, pending_push, event_recycle, error_message<br>• `:322` native real-allocation sweep: fail the k-th `operator new` on the destructor, drain and synchronize paths, prefill 0..23 and 1024 | `oom_sync` **rc -6** `terminate called after throwing an instance of 'std::bad_alloc'` (both conditions; gdb: `_Deque_base::_M_allocate_map` inside `sync_and_release_all_impl`) | no GPU: **rc 0** `PASS: allocation failure propagated safely`.<br>GPU: **rc -6** after `PASS: nonallocating completion path`, in pybind11 teardown (D4).<br>Disarm variant: **rc 0** in both conditions. |
